gy/reference/bem_new.html","id":"ref-usage","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Usage","title":"Create a new object with BEM data — bem_new","text":"","code":"bem_new(CP, CA, CB, CTM, CTO, CQ, ACT, RA, RB, RTM, RTO, RQ, FA, UA, SDA, ED)"},{"path":"https://bomeara.github.io/fishyenergy/reference/bem_new.html","id":"arguments","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Arguments","title":"Create a new object with BEM data — bem_new","text":"CP proportion maximum consumption CA intercept allometric mass function CB slope allometric mass function; negative bc bigger fish consume less per gram body mass smaller fish CTM critical thermal maximum (degrees C) CTO laboratory temperature preferendum (degrees C)= CQ approximates Q10; rate function increases relatively low water temperatures ACT activity coefficient RA intercept allometric activity function RB slope allometric activity function RTM critical thermal maximum (degrees C) RTO laboratory temperature preferendum (degrees C) RQ approximates Q10; rate function increases relatively low water temperatures FA fish body mass (grams) UA activity (mg/kg-day) SDA salinity (psu) ED energy density (J/kg)","code":""},{"path":"https://bomeara.github.io/fishyenergy/reference/bem_new.html","id":"value","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Value","title":"Create a new object with BEM data — bem_new","text":"BEM object","code":""},{"path":"https://bomeara.github.io/fishyenergy/reference/compute_single_station.html","id":null,"dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Compute growth for a year at a station — single_station_compute","title":"Compute growth for a year at a station — single_station_compute","text":"Compute growth year station","code":""},{"path":"https://bomeara.github.io/fishyenergy/reference/compute_single_station.html","id":"ref-usage","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Usage","title":"Compute growth for a year at a station — single_station_compute","text":"","code":"